## rule: leetspeak reversed (de-leet / normalize)
## source: hashcat-7.1/rules/leetspeak.rule, each `sXY` reversed to `sYX`
## purpose: map leet characters back to their plain letter
## example: j0hn ---> john
## note: leetspeak.rule maps both g->9 (sg9) and q->9 (sq9). The reverse is
##       ambiguous for '9'; we keep 9->g (first occurrence) and drop 9->q.

s4a
s@a
s6b
s<c
s{c
s3e
s9g
s1i
s!i
s0o
s5s
s$s
s7t
s+t
s%x
